## Vendored source

**termux-x11** — https://github.com/termux/termux-x11 — GPL-3.0
Included as a git submodule at `vendor/termux-x11`, unmodified. The `lorie`
module is the X server that renders the desktop; `shell-loader` provides the
guest-side `Loader` class and the Android internal-API stubs it compiles
against. Upstream deliberately parameterised the embedding, which is why no
fork was needed.

## Bundled binaries

Taken from the Termux package repository (https://packages.termux.dev), pinned
by version and SHA-256 in `tools/native/native.lock.json`.

| Component | Upstream | Licence |
|---|---|---|
| proot (and its loader) | https://github.com/termux/proot | GPL-2.0-or-later |
| busybox | https://git.busybox.net/busybox | GPL-2.0 |
| libtalloc | https://gitlab.com/samba-team/samba | LGPL-3.0-or-later |
| libandroid-shmem | https://github.com/termux/libandroid-shmem | MIT |
| libandroid-selinux | https://github.com/termux/termux-packages | Public domain |
| PCRE2 | https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2 | BSD-3-Clause |

`tools/native/fetch.py` renames and re-links these; the transformation is
described in `docs/native-binaries.md`. No source is modified.

## Downloaded at runtime

Debian system images are pulled from the Docker Hub `library/debian` repository
at install time and are not redistributed with the app. Debian is a trademark of
Software in the Public Interest, Inc.

## Design owed to proot-distro

The proot invocation — the extension flags, the bind list, the fake `/proc`
contents — was read from `proot-distro` 5.8.0 (https://github.com/termux/proot-distro,
GPL-3.0) and reimplemented in Kotlin. The fake `/proc` file contents in
`core/.../runtime/SysData.kt` are copied from its `sysdata.py` byte for byte.

